{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"80\t## Fabrication contract (per target adapter)\n81\t\n82\t- Pin the CLI versions the writer was validated against; on an unknown version\n83\t  warn and offer bootstrap.\n84\t- Write only new session files under the CLI's own session directory; never\n85\t  modify existing native sessions.\n86\t- Represent foreign tool calls faithfully (or as clearly-labeled text when the\n87\t  target rejects unknown tool schemas — see per-adapter spec notes).\n88\t- Propagate the source model id into fabricated assistant envelopes verbatim\n89\t  (decided 2026-07-21). If the target harness recognizes it — e.g. the user\n90\t  registered matching external models in Claude Code — the session restores\n91\t  seamlessly; otherwise the target warns once and falls back to its default,\n92\t  which is accurate (\"this bridge changed models\"). Never substitute a\n93\t  recognized-but-false id.\n94\t\n95\tReverse-engineered, empirically verified format specs (pinned versions,\n96\tminimal working schemas, unknowns): [docs/specs/claude-session-format.md](specs/claude-session-format.md),\n97\t[docs/specs/codex-rollout-format.md](specs/codex-rollout-format.md), and\n98\t[docs/specs/opencode-session-format.md](specs/opencode-session-format.md).\n99\tKey constraints: Claude resume is scoped to the project dir encoded from the\n100\tlaunch cwd and reconstructs history by walking `parentUuid` from the last\n101\tline; Codex resume-by-id scans `~/.codex/sessions` for a matching filename +\n102\t`session_meta` id, and only plain `message` response_items are verified-safe\n103\tto replay (foreign tool calls fold into labeled text). Claude accepts foreign\n104\t`tool_use` names verbatim, so Codex→Claude keeps structured tool history.\n105\t\n106\topencode is the first target that breaks the \"write a new session file\"\n107\tassumption: every session lives in one shared SQLite DB, so fabrication builds\n108\ta payload in opencode's own export format and shells out to `opencode import`.\n109\tThree consequences the file-based targets don't have. Import is **not atomic**\n110\t— a payload rejected part-way leaves a truncated session behind, so a failed\n111\timport deletes it before falling back to bootstrap. Message order comes from\n112\t`time.created` rather than payload position, so the import notice is backdated\n113\tahead of history instead of stamped `now` (stamped `now`, it sorted last and\n114\trendered as a `QUEUED` prompt). And `info.projectID` — an opaque id looked up\n115\tvia `opencode debug scrap`, not derivable from the path — is what scopes a\n116\tsession to a repo; the `global` fallback lists it from every directory.\n117\t\n118\t## Sharing model\n119\t\n120\t`actor.id`/`actor.display` come from `git config user.email/name` at capture\n121\ttime. Default listings: own + unattributed conversations; `--all` shows every\n122\tauthor with labels. Transport is optional-but-default-on: Conversation\n123\tLedger's auto-installed pre-push hook and fetch refspec ride normal\n124\t`git push`/`git fetch`, gated by the ledger's secret scan and disableable per\n125\tuser (`{\"transport\": {\"hook\": false, \"fetchRefspec\": false}}`); `cledger sync`\n126\tremains available for an explicit push/fetch/merge. Turnbridge adds no\n127\tnetwork behavior of its own — it only reads whatever the ledger has already\n128\tabsorbed locally. Events captured before identity stamping existed are\n129\tunattributed; a forced transcript rescan after the upgrade can duplicate\n130\tthose turns under new event ids.\n131\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y2t9bC8ZjfDTR6vihyu7CQ","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","dirty_fingerprint":"bc65e878d80c1722a0adee9428cbf850f1d73e21ecfd82d0c4182876ebf93c10","head":"173cfc66bb28f4c20e474f522f197eeef0c627de","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turn