code\"` in an import payload, changing nothing else, makes","+the model respond **and correctly recall a marker planted in the bridged","+history**. So fabrication itself is sound — the model does read the history.","+","+Your job is to fix this properly, which means resolving the tension rather than","+just hardcoding `\"opencode\"`: the provider/model must be resolvable by opencode","+so the session can be continued, while the source model's identity is still","+preserved somewhere honest (the import notice text is one option). Do not","+silently claim the bridged turns were produced by a model that did not produce","+them. State your chosen approach in the PR.","+","+One more observation, **unconfirmed**, worth investigating while you are here:","+after the provider fix, the recall run answered correctly and then kept","+regenerating — ~237 repetitions of the marker with filler like \"The loop has","+resumed\" — until the process was killed. That may be nothing more than a small","+free model degenerating, but it may also be structural: fabricated assistant","+messages carry only a `text` part, where native ones carry `step-start` …","+`step-finish` around it, so opencode's loop may never see a terminal state.","+Determine which. If it is structural, fix it; if it is just the model, say so","+and move on. Guard the probe with a timeout either way so it cannot hang.","+","+So this task has **two deliverables**: the probe, and a fix. A probe that","+correctly reports FAIL is not sufficient — the point is a fabricated opencode","+session you can actually talk to.","+"," Requirements:"," "," 1. Seed a two-turn conversation into a throwaway git repo via"],"newLines":56,"newStart":43,"oldLines":21,"oldStart":43}],"userModified":false},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"6e5359a1-826c-4fc0-b428-0a9813ebc5a9","version":"2.1.223"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-08-06T04:41:56.123Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
