{"actor":{"id":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","type":"agent"},"content":{"agent":"Explore","blocks":[{"text":"## Intent Recall Exploration Report\n\n**Purpose:**\nIntent Recall is an evidence-backed retrieval system designed to help humans and AI agents find historical proof of intended behavior in repositories. It inspects recorded conversations, decisions, specifications, code, and tests to answer \"what behavior was actually intended?\" The system distinguishes original requests from later changes of mind and exposes underlying evidence with full provenance, treating each implementation artifact as a lossy expression of human goals.\n\n**Relationship to Conversation Ledger & Turnbridge:**\nIntent Recall is fundamentally a **consumer** of Conversation Ledger data. It reads immutable events directly from the shared ledger to build derived, versioned indexes. Turnbridge is explicitly identified as \"one valuable producer of conversational evidence,\" but Intent Recall is designed to support decisions arriving through multiple ingestion paths—not exclusively Turnbridge. This establishes a clear division:\n- **Turnbridge**: Captures CLI session transcripts as conversation events in Conversation Ledger\n- **Intent Recall**: Reads from Conversation Ledger (plus other evidence sources) to retrieve and structure intent evidence\n\nThe systems share the Conversation Ledger as their data model bridge.\n\n**Design Constraints on Conversation Event Storage:**\n\n1. **Immutability & Addressability**: All events must be immutable with permanent event IDs, allowing raw evidence to remain directly addressable. Derived indexes reference exact event IDs and excerpts.\n\n2. **Evidence Granularity**: An open design question is source-link granularity—should citations point to turns, paragraphs, sentences, or spans? This directly affects how fine-grained conversation events need to be segmented.\n\n3. **Metadata Requirements**: Each conversational event should support:\n   - Chronological ordering and timestamping\n   - Actor identification (who made requests/decisions)\n   - Explicit supersession relationships (when later events override earlier ones)\n   - Contradiction detection and tracking\n\n4. **Structured Claims over Raw Conversations**: While raw conversations are preserved, Intent Recall derives structured annotations tracking actors, requested behaviors, constraints, acceptance criteria, scope, and supersession. Each derived claim requires source links, confidence scores, and extractor/version provenance.\n\n5. **Distinction Between Evidence Types**: The model classifies evidence as:\n   - Human requests and clarifications\n   - Accepted/rejected decisions and their chronology\n   - Specifications and documentation\n   - Tests and code (treated as implementation artifacts, not unquestioned intent)\n\nThis means conversation events should preserve conversational context richly enough to retroactively classify whether a message represents a human request, decision ratification, or clarification.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","dirty_fingerprint":"bc65e878d80c1722a0adee9428cbf850f1d73e21ecfd82d0c4182876ebf93c10","head":"173cfc66bb28f4c20e474f522f197eeef0c627de","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e#agent:a49750c41a1d47ca5","parent":"claude-code:c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","seq":19},"id":"ev1-680d9b36253b3ae58d1650861c5aee1e5a8fe0fa9a9796c6e60364015178386e","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-19T06:35:48.409Z","producer":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","session_id":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.215","tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"agentId":"a49750c41a1d47ca5","attributionAgent":"Explore","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","entrypoint":"cli","gitBra