{"actor":{"id":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","type":"agent"},"content":{"agent":"Explore","blocks":[{"text":"## Sticky-note Exploration Report\n\n### 1. **Purpose**\nSticky-note is **git-backed shared memory for human-to-human handoff between AI coding assistants**. It captures what happens in each session (files touched, work type, narrative, failed approaches) and surfaces this context to teammates automatically on their next session—making implicit knowledge explicit without changing how anyone works. Currently at v3.0.0, MIT licensed, ~6.3K lines of Node.js hook code.\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Architecture Overview**\n\n**Session Capture Pipeline:**\n- **Hooks at lifecycle events**: `SessionStart` → `SessionEnd` (Claude Code) or `sessionStart` → `sessionEnd` per turn (Copilot CLI)\n- **Per-prompt injection**: `UserPromptSubmit`/`userPromptSubmitted` scores open threads by relevance (file overlap, branch match, recency)\n- **Tool tracking**: `PostToolUse` appends JSONL audit entries (file, tool name, session ID) for every tool call\n- **Error capture**: `PostToolUseFailure` marks threads as stuck and records failed approaches\n\n**Data Storage:**\n- **Thread state**: `.sticky-note/sticky-note.json` (git-tracked) — one JSON object with `threads[]` array, each with ID, user, status, files_touched, narrative, failed_approaches, resume_chain, contributors\n- **Per-user audit logs**: `.sticky-note/audit/{username}.jsonl` — one file per team member, JSONL format with tool_use entries\n- **Presence tracking**: `.sticky-note/presence/{username}.json` — active files per developer\n- **Signal files**: `.sticky-resume`, `.sticky-session`, `.sticky-head` (local only, git-ignored) for session continuity and resume coordination\n\n**Transcript Parsing:**\n- `parse-transcript.js` handles both JSONL (Claude Code transcript) and plaintext (fallback)\n- Extracts narrative: last assistant message (300 char max)\n- Detects failed approaches: combines ERROR_PATTERNS regex + RETRY_PATTERNS to identify error→retry sequences\n- Handles tool_use entries to extract files touched from tool inputs\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Supported CLIs & Transcript Formats**\n\n| CLI | Format | Discovery | Resume |\n|-----|--------|-----------|--------|\n| **Claude Code** | JSONL transcript + hook input | SessionStart/SessionEnd hooks (per-session) | `.sticky-resume` signal file + `resume-thread` CLI |\n| **Copilot CLI** | Reconstructed from audit trail (no direct transcript access) | `sessionStart`/`sessionEnd` per turn + hook env vars | Same as Claude Code, works cross-CLI |\n| **Codex** | Plaintext stdout/stderr captured via bash wrapper | Post-session `sticky-codex.sh` wrapper | Via MCP server only |\n| **MCP Clients** (Cursor, Windsurf, etc.) | N/A — read-only via 8-tool MCP server | Via `get_thread_context_for_files()` MCP tool | Via `get_session_context()` MCP tool |\n\n**Key discovery mechanisms:**\n- `sticky-note.json` stores all threads with full metadata\n- `.sticky-note/audit/*.jsonl` provides session-level detail\n- `git blame` integration for file→thread attribution (V2.5+)\n- `resume-thread --query \"topic\"` does text similarity search across narratives/failed_approaches\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Directly Reusable Code**\n\n**parse-transcript.js** (67 lines) — Production-ready transcript extraction:\n- Handles JSONL + plaintext formats\n- ERROR_PATTERNS & RETRY_PATTERNS regex for failed approach detection\n- Exports `extractNarrativeFromEntries()`, `extractFailedFromEntries()` \n\n**sticky-utils.js** (1,132 lines) — Comprehensive session utilities:\n- Path resolution (`getMemoryPath()`, `getAuditDir()`)\n- JSON I/O with git merge strategy (`saveMemoryMerged()`)\n- Thread search & filtering (`findThreadById()`)\n- Audit trail querying (`extractSessionFromAudit()`)\n- Git blame integration for attribution\n\n**sticky-attribution.js** (534 lines) — File→thread mapping:\n- Runs `git blame --line-porcelain` per file\n- Three-tier SHA resolution (Git Notes → Audit JSONL → file+date heuristic)\n- Returns line ranges for context injection\n\n**bin/mcp-server.js** (partial) — Inter-tool communication:\n- 8 MCP tools: `get_session_context()`, `search_threads()`, `check_overlaps()`, `get_thread_context_for_files()`\n- Zero external dependencies\n- Stdio JSON-RPC 2.0 protocol\n\n**session-end.js capture logic** (1,021 lines):\n- Extracts files touched from transcript tool_use entries + git diff\n- Classifies work type via activity patterns\n- Computes resume_chain for cross-tool continuity\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Tech Stack & Maturity**\n\n- **Language**: Node.js >= 16 (pure JS, no TypeScript)\n- **Dependencies**: Zero — uses only Node.js built-ins (fs, path, child_process, crypto)\n- **Storage**: Git repository (branch-independent via orphan branch in v3.0.0)\n- **Data format**: JSON for threads, JSONL for audit logs\n- **Size**: ~6,300 lines of hook code across 12 files\n- **Maturity**: Actively maintained, v3.0.0 recent (data-branch refactor), 50+ commits in last cycle\n- **Testing**: Smoke test suite exists\n\n**Architecture decisions relevant to Turnbridge:**\n- Avoids external service: Everything stored locally in git\n- CLI-agnostic thread format: Same data structure works across Claude Code, Copilot CLI, Codex\n- Multi-layer context injection: Static instructions + per-session + per-prompt + MCP tools gives resilience if one channel fails\n- Git merge strategy: `.gitattributes merge=union` + UUID threads avoid conflicts on concurrent pushes","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","dirty_fingerprint":"bc65e878d80c1722a0adee9428cbf850f1d73e21ecfd82d0c4182876ebf93c10","head":"173cfc66bb28f4c20e474f522f197eeef0c627de","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e#agent:a264be797d1ae6615","parent":"claude-code:c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","seq":68},"id":"ev1-558a836c4ca2f68363791243d3