{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"# Codex Rollout Format Implementation in `casr`\n\nBased on the repository documentation, here are the key findings:\n\n## Source File Locations\n\nThe README identifies Codex session handling in `src/providers/codex.rs` (implied from the provider trait architecture). The exact path structure isn't explicitly listed, but the documentation references:\n\n- Provider implementation files follow pattern: `src/providers/<provider>.rs`\n- Tests likely exist in `tests/` directory\n\n## Codex Session Schema\n\nAccording to the documentation, the Codex rollout format operates as follows:\n\n**Storage Pattern:**\n`~/.codex/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/rollout-N.jsonl`\n\n**Event Types Constructed:**\nThe writer emits multiple record variants:\n- `session_meta` events (session initialization)\n- `response_item` records (assistant responses)\n- Token-count events (when available)\n\n**Core Fields:**\nThe documentation states: \"JSONL events include `session_meta`, `response_item`, and `event_msg` variants.\"\n\n## Implementation Approach\n\nThe `casr` system uses a provider-agnostic trait model where each provider (including Codex) implements:\n- `read_session()` — parsing native JSONL to canonical format\n- `write_session()` — generating provider-plausible JSONL with expected fields and timestamps\n\nThe actual file paths for implementation sources aren't directly exposed in the public README content provided.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01NBEnZSDVxtaAN7cx2iNGno","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","dirty_fingerprint":"bc65e878d80c1722a0adee9428cbf850f1d73e21ecfd82d0c4182876ebf93c10","head":"173cfc66bb28f4c20e474f522f197eeef0c627de","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e#agent:add0fb660669a74c5","parent":"claude-code:c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","seq":112},"