{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"# Git AI Project Overview\n\n## What It Does\nGit AI is an open-source extension that automatically tracks AI-generated code in repositories. As stated in the project: \"every line of AI code is linked to the **agent, model, and prompts** that generated it.\"\n\n## How It Captures AI Agent Sessions\nThe system works through a three-step process:\n1. Coding agents call `git-ai checkpoint` when writing or modifying code\n2. On commit, Git AI stores line-level attribution data in Git Notes\n3. The tool preserves attributions during Git operations like rebase, squash, and cherry-pick\n\nNotably, Git AI doesn't use AI detection—agents explicitly report which lines they created, ensuring accurate attribution.\n\n## Supported Agents\nThe project supports numerous agents including Claude Code, GitHub Copilot, Cursor, Codex, OpenCode, Windsurf, Droid, Amp, Gemini, Continue, and others. An extensible framework allows adding new agents.\n\n## GitHub Stars\nThe repository has **2.3k stars** and 238 forks as of the snapshot date.\n\n## Conversation Resumption Support\nThe documentation provided contains no information about resuming or rehydrating conversations across different CLI tools. This capability is not mentioned or documented in the available content.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01JTYBmk2TdcgA5326SdRefC","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","dirty_fingerprint":"bc65e878d80c1722a0adee9428cbf850f1d73e21ecfd82d0c4182876ebf93c10","head":"173cfc66bb28f4c20e474f522f197eeef0c627de","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e#agent:adb79c2086870a6d6","parent":"claude-code:c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","seq":22},"id":"ev1-ba9cbb2b4327a79be583568c10ee7adb4c9cd89091f6fc91dc21e9caed9b71b5","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-19T06:36:03.315Z","pro