{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t# Product intent\n2\t\n3\t## Purpose\n4\t\n5\tTurnbridge lets a developer continue a visible coding conversation in a\n6\tdifferent agent CLI when they choose to switch providers or tools. It retains\n7\tthe full user-visible turn history—messages, tool calls, and tool results—\n8\trather than requiring a last-minute summary from a rate-limited model.\n9\t\n10\tIt serves two users who are often the same person on different days: a solo\n11\tdeveloper hopping CLIs mid-task (rate limits, model choice), and small\n12\tcollaborating groups whose members use *different* CLIs and want to pick up\n13\teach other's conversations. Sharing rides on Conversation Ledger's git-notes\n14\tstorage; each turn is attributed to its human author via the repo's git\n15\tidentity, and listings show only your own (plus unattributed) conversations\n16\tunless you ask for everyone's.\n17\t\n18\t## Behavioral commitments\n19\t\n20\t- Capture every available visible turn incrementally, not only on clean exit\n21\t  (delivered by Conversation Ledger's hooks; see division below).\n22\t- Preserve source content faithfully and label its originating CLI.\n23\t- Offer one resume picker across supported CLIs while making the session type\n24\t  honest: native resume for same-CLI records, native-format fabrication for\n25\t  cross-CLI records, transcript rehydration as the always-available fallback.\n26\t- Prefer conversations whose repository and code state match the current work;\n27\t  warn rather than silently treating mismatched history as current.\n28\t- Never claim to transfer hidden reasoning, private provider state, or an\n29\t  exact native session; a fabricated session is labeled as imported.\n30\t- Put the developer in control of capture, sharing, and deletion. Sharing is\n31\t  a deliberate choice, not a side effect: today it is an explicit\n32\t  `cledger sync`; the decided direction (see Conversation Ledger's design\n33\t  doc) is optional-but-default-on transport hooks so records ride normal\n34\t  `git push`/`pull`, gated by the ledger's secret scan and disableable per\n35\t  user. Listings default to the current user's records.\n36\t\n37\t## Non-goals\n38\t\n39\t- A team presence system, task tracker, or agent orchestration framework.\n40\t- Inferring or replacing human intent.\n41\t- Summarized \"handoff notes\" (sticky-note-style); Turnbridge moves the literal\n42\t  record.\n43\t\n44\t## Relationship to Conversation Ledger\n45\t\n46\tTurnbridge is a client of Conversation Ledger, which owns the durable neutral\n47\trecord **and** the source-CLI capture adapters (hooks, transcript parsers,\n48\tcursors, dedup). Turnbridge owns everything on the resume side: the unified\n49\tpicker, ownership/compatibility filtering, target-CLI session fabrication,\n50\tbootstrap rehydration, and the optional command shims.\n51\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_01E7MPFv5WpHNTwi7gGHsFkx","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","dirty_fingerprint":"bc65e878d80c1722a0adee9428cbf850f1d73e21ecfd82d0c4182876ebf93c10","head":"173cfc66bb28f4c20e474f522f197eeef0c627de","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:6b979ed9-e38e-4fea-b585-342bba5a333c#agent:a00a6de33281486a4","parent":"claude-code:6b979ed9-e38e-4fea-b585-342bba5a333c","seq":7},"id":"ev1-bb05b3b1d95a291eef93edc236b7439bb5cc3317404c35c60fd7c019e7449e06","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-21T22:09:20.490Z","producer":{"session_id":"6b979ed9-e38e-4fea-b585-342bba5a333c","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.216","tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"agentId":"a00a6de33281486a4","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":true,"message":{"content":[{"content":"1\t# Product intent\n2\t\n3\t## Purpose\n4\t\n5\tTurnbridge lets a developer 