{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t# Thread resume — local mode (V2.5)\n2\t\n3\tThread resume lets one developer pick up where another left off.\n4\tAlice's thread becomes Bob's active thread — one thread, two\n5\tcontributors, continuous audit trail.\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## Quick Start\n10\t\n11\t```bash\n12\t# Search by topic\n13\tnpx sticky-note resume-thread --query \"auth refresh sliding window\"\n14\t\n15\t# Search by user\n16\tnpx sticky-note resume-thread --user alice\n17\t\n18\t# Combined: topic + user + file context\n19\tnpx sticky-note resume-thread --query \"auth fix\" --user alice --file src/auth/refresh.ts\n20\t\n21\t# Natural language (positional query)\n22\tnpx sticky-note resume-thread \"pick up where Alice left off on auth\"\n23\t\n24\t# JSON output (for MCP tool integration)\n25\tnpx sticky-note resume-thread --query \"auth\" --json\n26\t```\n27\t\n28\t---\n29\t\n30\t## How it works\n31\t\n32\t### 1. Thread discovery\n33\t\n34\t`resume-thread` searches all non-expired threads using:\n35\t\n36\t- Text similarity — matches query against narrative, failed_approaches,\n37\t  handoff_summary, last_note, and files_touched\n38\t- User filter — optional, filters to a specific thread author\n39\t- File attribution — boosts threads whose attributed lines (via\n40\t  built-in `git blame`) overlap with the specified file\n41\t\n42\t### 2. Match selection\n43\t\n44\t- If one clear winner: selected automatically\n45\t- If top 2 scores are within 0.5 of each other: both shown, best selected\n46\t- JSON mode returns best_match + alternatives for programmatic use\n47\t\n48\t### 3. Resume activation\n49\t\n50\tWhen a thread is resumed:\n51\t\n52\t1. `.sticky-resume` signal file is written (for session-start hook)\n53\t2. `.sticky-active-resume` marker is written (for session-end hook)\n54\t3. Next AI session picks up the thread's full context automatically\n55\t4. Session-end appends to the resumed thread (not a new thread)\n56\t\n57\t### 4. Thread update on session end\n58\t\n59\tWhen Bob's session ends on a resumed thread:\n60\t\n61\t- `contributors[]` is updated: `[\"alice\", \"bob\"]`\n62\t- `resumed_by` is set to `\"bob\"`\n63\t- `resumed_at` is timestamped\n64\t- `resume_history[]` gets a new entry\n65\t- Files touched, narrative, prompts are merged into Alice's thread\n66\t\n67\t---\n68\t\n69\t## Thread schema additions (V2.5)\n70\t\n71\tAll fields are **optional and backward-compatible** — V1/V2 threads work\n72\tunchanged.\n73\t\n74\t| Field | Type | Description |\n75\t|-------|------|-------------|\n76\t| `contributors` | `string[]` | All users who have worked on this thread |\n77\t| `resumed_by` | `string` | Most recent user to resume this thread |\n78\t| `resumed_at` | `string` | ISO timestamp of most recent resume |\n79\t| `resume_history` | `object[]` | Full chain: `{ user, at, session_id }` |\n80\t\n81\tExample thread with resume data:\n82\t\n83\t```json\n84\t{\n85\t  \"id\": \"9c2a2b01-...\",\n86\t  \"user\": \"alice\",\n87\t  \"contributors\": [\"alice\", \"bob\"],\n88\t  \"resumed_by\": \"bob\",\n89\t  \"resumed_at\": \"2026-03-07T14:22:00Z\",\n90\t  \"resume_history\": [\n91\t    { \"user\": \"bob\", \"at\": \"2026-03-07T14:22:00Z\", \"session_id\": \"def-456\" }\n92\t  ],\n93\t  \"resume_chain\": [\n94\t    { \"session_id\": \"abc-123\", \"tool\": \"claude-code\", ... },\n95\t    { \"session_id\": \"def-456\", \"tool\": \"copilot-cli\", ... }\n96\t  ]\n97\t}\n98\t```\n99\t\n100\t---\n101\t\n102\t## Injection vs resume\n103\t\n104\t| | Injection | Resume |\n105\t|---|-----------|--------|\n106\t| **Context** | Read-only background | Active thread |\n107\t| **Thread** | Unchanged | Appended to |\n108\t| **Contributors** | Not updated | Updated |\n109\t| **New thread created?** | No | No — same thread |\n110\t| **Audit trail** | Separate session | Continuous |\n111\t\n112\t---\n113\t\n114\t## Limitation: push required\n115\t\n116\tIn V2.5, `resume-thread` reads `sticky-note.json` and audit JSONL\n117\t**locally**. If Alice is on a different machine and hasn't pushed, her\n118\tthreads are not visible to Bob.\n119\t\n120\t**Workaround:** Alice pushes her branch. Bob pulls. Resume works.\n121\t\n122\t**Workaround:** Ensure both developers push/pull regularly so thread\n123\tdata stays in sync.\n124\t\n125\t---\n126\t\n127\t## What resume is not\n128\t\n129\t- ✗ Not a fork — one thread, multiple contributors\n130\t- ✗ Not an assignment — Bob pulls, Alice doesn't push\n131\t- ✗ Not a lock — Alice can resume her own thread concurrently\n132\t- ✗ Not required — smart injection still works without resume\n133\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_013ws1oAzPMpZBgBNyMtfpJS","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","dirty_fingerprint":"bc65e878d80c1722a0adee9428cbf850f1d73e21ecfd82d0c4182876ebf93c10","head":"173cfc66bb28f4c20e474f522f197eeef0c627de","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e#agent:a264be797d1ae6615","parent":"claude-code:c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","seq":49},"id":"ev1-ed3e547d8a9f4f3955d38c827f5bbff36d8f60c5cdfdf2c0e057fd1623fd5385","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-19T06:36:05.000Z","producer":{"session_id":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.215","tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"agentId":"a264be797d1ae6615","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":true,"message":{"content":[{"content":"1\t# Thread resume — local mode (V2.5)\n2\t\n3\tThread resume lets one developer pick up where another left off.\n4\tAlice's thread becomes Bob's active thread — one thread, two\n5\tcontributors, continuous audit trail.\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## Quick Start\n10\t\n11\t```bash\n12\t# Search by topic\n13\tnpx sticky-note resume-thread --query \"auth ref