ontinuous |\n\n---\n\n## Limitation: push required\n\nIn V2.5, `resume-thread` reads `sticky-note.json` and audit JSONL\n**locally**. If Alice is on a different machine and hasn't pushed, her\nthreads are not visible to Bob.\n\n**Workaround:** Alice pushes her branch. Bob pulls. Resume works.\n\n**Workaround:** Ensure both developers push/pull regularly so thread\ndata stays in sync.\n\n---\n\n## What resume is not\n\n- ✗ Not a fork — one thread, multiple contributors\n- ✗ Not an assignment — Bob pulls, Alice doesn't push\n- ✗ Not a lock — Alice can resume her own thread concurrently\n- ✗ Not required — smart injection still works without resume\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/repos/BandaruDheeraj/sticky-note/docs/thread-resume.md","numLines":133,"startLine":1,"totalLines":133},"type":"text"},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"878073e9-4a23-4d9b-9900-20052d3ddb47","version":"2.1.215"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-08-11T02:16:46.077Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t# Turnbridge\n2\t\n3\tLossless visible-conversation continuity between coding agent CLIs.\n4\t\n5\t[Conversation Ledger](https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger)\n6\tcaptures native local transcripts (Claude Code, Codex) incrementally into git\n7\tnotes. Turnbridge is the resume layer on top: one picker across CLIs, honest\n8\tsession typing, and rehydration of a conversation into a *different* CLI —\n9\twithout claiming to transfer hidden reasoning or provider-private state.\n10\t\n11\t## Usage\n12\t\n13\t```sh\n14\t# capture (once per machine): conversation-ledger hooks\n15\tcledger install all\n16\t\n17\t# pick a conversation from this repo's history and resume it anywhere\n18\tturnbridge resume            # interactive: choose conversation, then target CLI\n19\tturnbridge resume codex      # resume straight into Codex\n20\tturnbridge resume claude     # resume straight into Claude Code\n21\tturnbridge list              # print compatible conversations\n22\t\n23\t# options\n24\t#   --all         include collaborators' conversations\n25\t#   --any-commit  include conversations from other branches/commits\n26\t#   --bootstrap   force transcript rehydration instead of native fabrication\n27\t\n28\t# optional: make bare `claude --resume` / `codex resume` open the merged picker\n29\tturnbridge shim install\n30\t```\n31\t\n32\tSame-CLI selections use the CLI's native resume. Cross-CLI selections write a\n33\ttarget-native session file and hand off to the target's own resume; when that\n34\tis unsupported for the installed CLI version, turnbridge falls back to a fresh\n35\tsession bootstrapped with the literal transcript.\n36\t\n37\tSee [product intent](docs/PRODUCT_INTENT.md) and the [WIP technical design](docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md).\n38\t\n39\t## Development\n40\t\n41\t```sh\n42\tnpm install   # links ../conversation-ledger\n43\tnpm test      # build + node --test\n44\t```\n45\t\n46\t## Licen