{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t# WIP technical design\n2\t\n3\t**Status:** exploratory; this is not yet an agent decision engine.\n4\t\n5\t## Evidence model\n6\t\n7\tIntent Recall consumes immutable events from Conversation Ledger and builds derived,\n8\tversioned indexes. Raw evidence always remains addressable. Derived claims must\n9\treference the exact event IDs and excerpts from which they were made.\n10\t\n11\tThe initial evidence classes are:\n12\t\n13\t- human requests and clarifications from visible conversations;\n14\t- accepted/rejected decisions and their chronology;\n15\t- specifications and documentation;\n16\t- tests and code, linked as implementation artifacts rather than treated as\n17\t  unquestioned intent.\n18\t\n19\t## Retrieval flow\n20\t\n21\tGiven a task, file, symbol, behavior, or question, Lens should:\n22\t\n23\t1. Resolve repository/code-state context.\n24\t2. Retrieve relevant raw evidence through lexical, structural, and eventually\n25\t   semantic indexes.\n26\t3. Group evidence by topic and chronology.\n27\t4. Detect explicit supersession or contradiction relationships.\n28\t5. Return a bounded evidence packet with citations, uncertainty, and an\n29\t   invitation to inspect the original material.\n30\t\n31\tAn agent-facing response must separate `evidence`, `inference`, and\n32\t`unresolved_questions`. It must never present a model-generated reconstruction\n33\tas a direct historical quote.\n34\t\n35\t## Structured intent (future)\n36\t\n37\tStructured claims may eventually model actors, requested behaviors,\n38\tconstraints, acceptance criteria, scope, and supersession. They are derived\n39\tannotations, not replacements for raw conversations. Each claim needs source\n40\tlinks, confidence, extractor/version provenance, and a review/correction path.\n41\t\n42\t## Open questions\n43\t\n44\t- What source-link granularity is useful: turn, paragraph, sentence, or span?\n45\t- How should current user instr