chnical design\n\n**Status:** exploratory; this is not yet an agent decision engine.\n\n## Evidence model\n\nIntent Recall consumes immutable events from Conversation Ledger and builds derived,\nversioned indexes. Raw evidence always remains addressable. Derived claims must\nreference the exact event IDs and excerpts from which they were made.\n\nThe initial evidence classes are:\n\n- human requests and clarifications from visible conversations;\n- accepted/rejected decisions and their chronology;\n- specifications and documentation;\n- tests and code, linked as implementation artifacts rather than treated as\n  unquestioned intent.\n\n## Retrieval flow\n\nGiven a task, file, symbol, behavior, or question, Lens should:\n\n1. Resolve repository/code-state context.\n2. Retrieve relevant raw evidence through lexical, structural, and eventually\n   semantic indexes.\n3. Group evidence by topic and chronology.\n4. Detect explicit supersession or contradiction relationships.\n5. Return a bounded evidence packet with citations, uncertainty, and an\n   invitation to inspect the original material.\n\nAn agent-facing response must separate `evidence`, `inference`, and\n`unresolved_questions`. It must never present a model-generated reconstruction\nas a direct historical quote.\n\n## Structured intent (future)\n\nStructured claims may eventually model actors, requested behaviors,\nconstraints, acceptance criteria, scope, and supersession. They are derived\nannotations, not replacements for raw conversations. Each claim needs source\nlinks, confidence, extractor/version provenance, and a review/correction path.\n\n## Open questions\n\n- What source-link granularity is useful: turn, paragraph, sentence, or span?\n- How should current user instructions interact with contradictory history?\n- Which sensitive evidence may be indexed or shown to a model?\n- How should branches, rebases, and renamed symbols affect relevance?\n- What evaluation set can measure faithful retrieval without rewarding\n  persuasive but unsupported synthesis?\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/intent-recall/docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":50},"type":"text"},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"d9308f7e-afc2-4e32-b23c-a1e24b666e8e","version":"2.1.215"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-08-11T02:16:46.202Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\n2\t# sticky-codex.sh — Codex wrapper for Sticky Note V2\n3\t#\n4\t# Captures Codex stdout/stderr to a temp session log.\n5\t# On exit: calls session-end.js with the transcript for\n6\t# narrative + failed_approaches extraction.\n7\t#\n8\t# Usage:\n9\t#   sticky-codex [codex args...]\n10\t#\n11\t# Setup:\n12\t#   npx sticky-note init --codex\n13\t#   alias sticky-codex=\"/path/to/.claude/hooks/sticky-codex.sh\"\n14\t#\n15\t# Limitation: Context is printed to terminal after Codex exits,\n16\t# not injected into the Codex window. Per-prompt surfacing not available.\n17\t\n18\tset -euo pipefail\n19\t\n20\tSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"\n21\tSTICKY_DIR=\"$(cd \"$SCRIPT_DIR/../..\" && pwd)/.sticky-note\"\n22\tSESSION_ID=\"codex-$(date +%s)-$$\"\n23\tTRANSCRIPT_FILE=$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/sticky-codex-XXXXXX.log\")\n24\tUSER=\"${USER:-${USERNAME:-unknown}}\"\n25\t\n26\t# Ensure .sticky-note directory exists\n27\tmkdir -p \"$STICKY_DIR\"\n28\t\n29\t# Print context from sticky-note before starting Codex\n30\techo \"\"\n31\techo \"📌 Sticky Note — injecting context for Codex session $SESSION_ID\"\n32\techo \"\"\n33\t\n34\tif [ -f \"$STICKY_DIR/sticky-note.json\" ]; then\n35\t    node \"$SCRIPT_DIR/session-start.js\" <<EOF 2>/dev/null || true\n36\t{\"session_id\": \"$SESSION_ID\"}\n37\tEOF\n38\tfi\n39\t\n40\techo \"─────────────────────────────────────────────\"\n41\techo \"\"\n42\t\n43\t# Run Codex, capturing output\n44\tcodex \"$@\" 2>&1 | tee \"$TRANSCRIPT_FILE\"\n45\tCODEX_EXIT=$?\n46\t\n47\techo \"\"\n48\techo \"─────────────────────────────────────────────\"\n49\techo \"📌 Sticky Note — processing Codex session...\"\n50\t\n51\t# Parse transcript for narrative + failed_approaches\n52\tPARSED=$(node \"$SCRIPT_DIR/parse-transcript.js\" \"$TRANSCRIPT_FILE\" 2>/dev/null || echo '{\"narrative\":\"\",\"failed_approaches\":[]}')\n53\t\n54\t# Call session-end.js with the transcript info + parsed data\n55\tnode \"$SCRIPT_DIR/session-end.js\" <<EOF 2>/dev/null || true\n56\t{\n57\t    \"session_id\": \"$SESSION_ID\",\n58\t    \"transcript_path\": \"$TRANSCRIPT_FILE\",\n59\t    \"parsed_transcript\": ${PARSED},\n60\t    \"hook_event_name\": \"sessionEnd\",\n61\t    \"reason\": \"codex_exit\"\n62\t}\n63\tEOF\n64\t\n65\t# Cleanup transcript\n66\trm -f \"$TRANSCRIPT_FILE\"\n67\t\n68\techo \"[OK] Session $SESSION_ID recorded.\"\n69\techo \"\"\n70\t\n71\texit $CODEX_EXIT\n72\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_01BNyA6Z4HxQttNUAFa79DDk","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","dirty_fingerprint":"bc65e878d80c1722a0adee9428cbf850f1d73e21ecfd82d0c4182876ebf93c10","head":"173cfc66bb28f4c20e474f522f197eeef0c627de","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e#agent:a264be797d1ae6615","parent":"claude-code:c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","seq":54},"id":"ev1-a52dccc396e5264aaf69a8f8472edb2bd7fc4696f17a7c6a07325761807f325b","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-19T06:36:09.550Z","producer":{"session_id":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.215","tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"agentId":"a264be797d1ae6615","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":true,"message":{"content":[{"content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\n2\t# sticky-codex.sh — Codex wrapper for Sticky Note V2\n3\t#\n4\t# Captures Codex stdout/stderr to a temp session log.\n5\t# On exit: calls session-end.js with the transcript for\n6\t# narrative + failed_approaches extraction.\n7\t#\n8\t# Usage:\n9\t#   sticky-codex [codex args...]\n10\t#\n11\t# Setup:\n12\t#   npx sticky-note init --codex\n13\t#   alias sticky-codex=\"/path/to/.claude/hooks/sticky-codex.sh\"\n14\t#\n15\t# Limitation: Context 