{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"=====54bb44b=====\ncommit 54bb44b1063c73b979f06c70ee95f032897b4841\nAuthor: Evin Tunador <evintunador@gmail.com>\nDate:   Mon Jul 20 16:06:03 2026 -0700\n\n    Fully mask matched span in scan/sync findings (0.6.1)\n    \n    Scan/sync finding excerpts no longer print any characters of the matched\n    secret — not even the leading-6/trailing-4 that the previous elided-middle\n    form (`supers…3456`) exposed. The match is replaced by a `<redacted>` marker\n    with ~20 chars of surrounding context preserved on each side, so a human\n    still gets a \"what was this\" cue while the report leaks zero secret bytes.\n    \n    This closes the sync-report channel of the capture/scan redaction feedback\n    loop: a captured scan report can no longer re-seed the very finding it\n    describes. Findings remain actionable via rule id + fingerprint (allow keys\n    on the fingerprint, redact on the event id), so nothing is lost operationally.\n    \n    Test tightened to slide a 6-char window across the whole secret and assert\n    none of those windows survive in the rendered finding.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n package.json          |  2 +-\n src/redact/scan.ts    | 21 ++++++++++++++-------\n src/test/scan.test.ts | 16 ++++++++++++++--\n 3 files changed, 29 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)\n=====33f522b=====\ncommit 33f522b9832b7de0b78d5f52e9cbb125d3f2403c\nAuthor: Evin Tunador <evintunador@gmail.com>\nDate:   Mon Jul 20 16:12:39 2026 -0700\n\n    Opt-in known-secrets store: capture learns confirmed secrets (0.7.0)\n    \n    Closes the capture side of the capture/scan redaction feedback loop. When\n    `{\"redact\": {\"knownSecrets\": true}}` is set (off by default), a\n    `cledger redact --pattern` remembers the exact values it scrubbed in a local\n    store, and capture-time redaction exact-matches them out of every future\n    event — so a value the broad sync scan caught but the conservative capture\n    tier missed can never be re-captured raw, and the fix-sync-fix churn can't\n    start.\n    \n    Design decisions (per discussion):\n    - Off by default. The store is never read or created unless the flag is on;\n      we don't silently record secrets somewhere users don't expect.\n    - The store holds plaintext values (fingerprints are one-way and can't drive\n      exact-match scrubbing) under .git/conversation-ledger/known-secrets.json.\n      .git/ is never tracked or pushed by git — structurally local and unshared,\n      the same tier as the allowlist, consistent with the transport trust\n      boundary.\n    - Only --pattern feeds the store (--all blanks whole content, no reusable\n      value); values shorter than 8 chars are never remembered, to avoid\n      exact-matching common short strings out of unrelated events.\n    - Scrubs are recorded under a distinct `known-secret` rule id, kept separate\n      from env-value masking in the audit trail via labeled extra-value groups.\n    \n    Note: like env masking, this makes capture machine-dependent for these\n    values (a teammate without the value in their store captures the same line\n    raw -> different event id).\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n package.json                   |   2 +-\n src/cli.ts                     |   6 ++\n src/redact/apply.ts            |  48 ++++++++++---\n src/redact/config.ts           |   7 ++\n src/redact/known-secrets.ts    |  71 +++++++++++++++++++\n src/store.ts                   |  57 ++++++++++++---\n src/test/known-secrets.test.ts | 154 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n src/test/redact.test.ts        |  24 ++++++-\n 8 files changed, 349 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)\n=====1ddda10=====\ncommit 1ddda1003ecda2e4821a3ee684226d0fa0fc9932\nAuthor: Evin Tunador <evintunador@gmail.com>\nDate:   Mon Jul 20 18:18:58 2026 -0700\n\n    Tighten keyword-assignment rule, lock store to 0600 (0.7.1)\n    \n    Two hardening fixes plus a latent test bug they exposed.\n    \n    1. keyword-assignment scan rule: the value charset now excludes code\n       punctuation — (){}[]<>;,$`\\ — alongside whitespace and quotes. Real\n       credentials are token-ish (alphanumerics plus -_.+/=~), whereas the dominant\n       false-positive class was source code that merely *talks* about secrets: type\n       annotations (`secret: string): string {`) and template interpolation\n       (`secret: ${secret.slice(i, i + 6)}`) now hit an excluded char immediately\n       and fall below the 8-char floor. Dogfooding this repo: 93 findings -> 64.\n       Secret-shaped string literals in fixtures still flag, correctly — those are\n       indistinguishable from the real thing by pattern alone.\n    \n    2. known-secrets store is written 0600 and repairs loosened perms on each\n       write (writeFile's mode only applies on create). It was landing 0644 —\n       world-readable — which is wrong for a file holding confirmed plaintext.\n    \n    3. Test isolation: helpers.ts now redirects HOME to a throwaway dir at module\n       load. loadConfig() reads ~/.config/cledger/config.json via os.homedir(), so\n       a developer with redact.knownSecrets enabled globally silently changed test\n       behavior — tests asserting *default* behavior exercised an opt-in layer and\n       failed. Tests must not depend on whose machine runs them.\n    \n    Docs: record the 0600 perms, note that a remembered value causes re-capture to\n    produce a new id (scrubbed copy, not a resurrected secret — id churn identical\n    to env masking), and fold the shipped items into the roadmap.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n README.md                      | 16 ++++++----------\n docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md   | 11 ++++++++---\n package.json                   |  2 +-\n src/redact/known-secrets.ts    | 25 ++++++++++++++++++++-----\n src/redact/rules.ts            | 17 ++++++++++++++++-\n src/test/helpers.ts            | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++\n src/test/known-secrets.test.ts | 20 +++++++++++++++++++-\n src/test/scan.test.ts          | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 8 files changed, 127 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)","is_error":false,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XuPvT1KuFnFRqPJUFqRvcy","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","dirty_fingerprint":"bc65e878d80c1722a0adee9428cbf850f1d73e21ecfd82d0c4182876ebf93c10","head":"173cfc66bb28f4c20e474f522f197eeef0c627de","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:6b979ed9-e38e-4fea-b585-342bba5a333c#agent:a5c627b890fdc1883","parent":"claude-code:6b979ed9-e38e-4fea-b585-342bba5a333c","seq":28},"id":"ev1-6e1d664fab602dafadc3b47985b7991e7add529747165dfa39712d37fb63a088","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-21T21:21:44.516Z","producer":{"session_id":"6b979ed9-e38e-4fea-b585-342bba5a333c","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.216","tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"agentId":"a5c627b890fdc1883","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":true,"message":{"content":[{"content":"=====54bb44b=====\ncommit 54bb44b1063c73b979f06c70ee95f032897b4841\nAuthor: Evin Tunador <evintunador@gmail.com>\nDate:   Mon Jul 20 16:06:03 2026 -0700\n\n    Fully mask matched span in scan/sync findings (0.6.1)\n    \n    Scan/sync finding excerpts no longer print any characters of the matched\n    secret — not even the leading-6/trailing-4 that the previous elided-middle\n    form (`supers…3456`) exposed. The match is replaced by a `<redacted>` marker\n    with ~20 chars of surrounding context preserved on each side, so a human\n    still gets a \"what was this\" cue while the report leaks zero secret bytes.\n    \n    This closes the sync-report channel of the capture/scan redaction feedback\n   