{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"=====d3934db=====\ncommit d3934db103de050d45d8db7e6e260e13e5907e27\nAuthor: Evin Tunador <evintunador@gmail.com>\nDate:   Mon Jul 20 23:26:22 2026 -0700\n\n    re_anchor events: mapping kind + read-time reachability resolution\n    \n    A re_anchor event asserts that commits rewritten away (squash merge,\n    history rewrite) live on in a successor commit. Anchored to the successor\n    so it rides the surviving branch's DAG; identity is deterministic\n    (sorted SHAs, system actor, successor's timestamp as occurred_at) so\n    independent detection on two machines dedups to one event. Read-time\n    reachability now resolves mappings to a fixpoint, so chained rewrites\n    (a squash commit itself squashed) revive transitively. appendEvents\n    grows an explicit-anchor option for this.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n src/index.ts              |   2 +\n src/reanchor.ts           |  93 ++++++++++++++++++++++\n src/schema.ts             |   1 +\n src/store.ts              |  71 +++++++++++++++--\n src/test/reanchor.test.ts | 195 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 5 files changed, 357 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)\n\n=====c36b4b5=====\ncommit c36b4b5569af37157237f4f433be6e5f8554d5e6\nAuthor: Evin Tunador <evintunador@gmail.com>\nDate:   Mon Jul 20 23:31:51 2026 -0700\n\n    Detect off-machine rewrites: patch-id/tree matching, auto-applied on read\n    \n    detectRewrites compares each local branch no longer reachable from the\n    remote default branch against the target's new first-parent commits:\n    tree equality catches a squash of an unmoved target, patch-id over\n    zero-context diffs catches squashes past unrelated drift and per-commit\n    rebase/bot rewrites. Only exact matches are proposed; two candidates\n    with the same fingerprint are reported as ambiguous, never guessed.\n    Branches with no noted commits are skipped. readEvents now runs the\n    pass lazily after absorbIncoming (default on, {\"reanchor\":{\"auto\":\n    false}} opts out), gated on a target-tip cursor and never throwing.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n src/index.ts                     |  12 ++-\n src/reanchor.ts                  | 228 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n src/redact/config.ts             |  15 ++-\n src/store.ts                     | 117 +++++++++++++++++++-\n src/test/reanchor-detect.test.ts | 201 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 5 files changed, 567 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)\n\n=====a452048=====\ncommit a452048571a5a075f6b32720b5f78ddfdc589098\nAuthor: Evin Tunador <evintunador@gmail.com>\nDate:   Mon Jul 20 23:33:59 2026 -0700\n\n    cledger re-anchor command: dry-run detection, --apply, manual --onto (0.8.0)\n    \n    Dry run is the default path; --apply appends the exact-match mappings.\n    The manual form (cledger re-anchor <old-rev...> --onto REV) covers what\n    mechanical matching cannot assert — maintainer-edited squashes, deleted\n    branches, ambiguous matches — with the asserting user as the actor.\n    Full 40-hex superseded SHAs are accepted verbatim even when the object\n    is already GC'd: the mapping is how an orphaned note stays meaningful.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n package.json                     |  2 +-\n src/cli.ts                       | 63 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n src/index.ts                     |  1 +\n src/reanchor.ts                  |  3 +-\n src/store.ts                     | 52 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n src/test/reanchor-detect.test.ts | 42 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-\n 6 files changed, 160 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)","is_error":false,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EQjMrAQFufpWbJDd134d8B","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","dirty_fingerprint":"bc65e878d80c1722a0adee9428cbf850f1d7