{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"Web search results for query: \"git-ai GitHub \"Git for the AI age\" acunniffe agent session\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - git-ai-project/git-ai: A Git extension for tracking the AI-generated code in your repos · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acunniffe/git-ai\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - agentsmill/age-of-agents: Age of Agents — watch your AI coding sessions grow a peaceful pixel-art realm. Run it with npx ai-of-agents.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/agentsmill/age-of-agents\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - open-gitagent/gitagent: A universal git-native AI agent framework. Your agent lives inside a git repo — identity, rules, memory, tools, and skills are all version-controlled files.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/open-gitagent/gitagent\"},{\"title\":\"GitAgentProtocol (GAP) — The Open Standard for Git-Native AI Agents\",\"url\":\"https://www.gitagent.sh/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - MAS-Infra-Layer/Agent-Git: Agent Git: Agent Version Control, Open-Branching, and Reinforcement Learning MDP for Agentic AI. A Standalone Agentic AI Infrastructure Layer for LangGraph Ecosystems · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/MAS-Infra-Layer/Agent-Git\"},{\"title\":\"Using Git with coding agents - Agentic Engineering Patterns - Simon Willison's Weblog\",\"url\":\"https://simonwillison.net/guides/agentic-engineering-patterns/using-git-with-coding-agents/\"},{\"title\":\"Git AI - Track AI Code all the way to production\",\"url\":\"https://usegitai.com/\"},{\"title\":\"Age of Agents — watch your AI coding sessions grow a peaceful pixel realm\",\"url\":\"https://agentsmill.github.io/age-of-agents/\"},{\"title\":\"git-ai/README.md at main · git-ai-project/git-ai\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/git-ai-project/git-ai/blob/main/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"Show HN: Git for AI Agents | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48063548\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about **git-ai**, a Git extension for the AI age:\n\n## Overview\n\ngit-ai is an open source git extension that tracks the AI-generated code in your repositories. The project is associated with the GitHub repository at acunniffe/git-ai.\n\n## Key Features\n\n**Attribution Tracking**: On commit, Git AI stores line-level attribution data in Git Notes, linking each line of AI-generated code to the agent, model, and session that created it. You can view this data by running `git log --show-notes=\"ai\"`.\n\n**Attribution Through Git Operations**: Git AI moves and merges line-level attributions when you squash, merge, reset, rebase, stash, cherry-pick, etc. so your AI code is always accurately tracked.\n\n**Accurate Detection**: Git AI does not use AI or heuristics to \"detect\" AI code — the Agents report exactly which lines they wrote, providing the most accurate, explicit attribution possible.\n\n## Usage\n\nGit AI works no matter how you commit — your Git client, the Git CLI, and your own Git aliases are all supported.\n\n## Enterprise Adoption\n\nHundreds of engineering teams (including many in the Fortune 100) use Git AI to understand their AI usage and make agents more effective on their codebase.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.","tool_use_id":"toolu_015wm3RbBwPyzwQ5coeCaWcQ","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","dirty_fingerprint":"bc65e878d80c1722a0adee9428cbf850f1d73e21ecfd82d0c4182876ebf93c10","head":"173cfc66bb28f4c20e474f522f197eeef0c627de","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e#agent:adb79c2086870a6d6","parent":"claude-code:c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","seq":12},"id":"ev1-6aba7c08321644c125bd9b0a44874f0641a4e69325ffb1e14c78b2345fa462fd","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-19T06:35:49.710Z","producer":{"session_id":"c158a6