{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"Web search results for query: \"resume Claude Code conversation in Codex CLI cross-agent portable transcript tool\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - hacktivist123/agent-session-resume: Cross-agent session resume skill for Claude Code, Codex, Antigravity, and OpenCode. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/hacktivist123/agent-session-resume\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Dicklesworthstone/cross_agent_session_resumer: Resume AI coding sessions across providers: converts Codex, Claude, Gemini, and other session formats through a canonical IR so you can pick up where you left off in any tool · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Dicklesworthstone/cross_agent_session_resumer\"},{\"title\":\"Codex CLI Resume, Continue, and Save Chat Explained - Verdent Guides\",\"url\":\"https://www.verdent.ai/guides/codex-cli-resume-continue-save-chat\"},{\"title\":\"Manage sessions - Claude Code Docs\",\"url\":\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sessions\"},{\"title\":\"[FEATURE] Allow resuming Claude Code sessions across devices · Issue #47926 · anthropics/claude-code\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/47926\"},{\"title\":\"Transfer Claude Code Sessions to OpenAI Codex and Gemini — One Command to Sync AI Agent Context | AuthSec Blog\",\"url\":\"https://authsec.ai/blogs/stop-re-explaining-bridge-claude-codex-gemini\"},{\"title\":\"Codex CLI Guide 2026: Setup, Sandbox, AGENTS.md & MCP\",\"url\":\"https://blakecrosley.com/guides/codex\"},{\"title\":\"Mastering Claude Code Sessions: –continue & –resume – AiOps School\",\"url\":\"https://aiopsschool.com/blog/mastering-claude-code-sessions-continue-resume/\"},{\"title\":\"Rses – cross-resume between Claude Code, Codex, and OpenCode | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47528990\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - yigitkonur/cli-continues: resume any AI coding session in another tool — Claude Code, Copilot, Gemini, Codex, Cursor\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/yigitkonur/cli-continues\"}]\n\nI found several relevant results about resuming Claude Code conversations in Codex CLI and cross-agent portable transcript tools. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n## Key Tools and Projects\n\n**agent-session-resume** is a reusable skill for continuing work from a prior AI coding-agent session without losing context, duplicating completed work, or overwriting unrelated changes. It is designed for handoffs between tools such as Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Antigravity, OpenCode, and GitHub Copilot.\n\n**cross_agent_session_resumer** provides a conversion pipeline that reads provider-specific native formats (Claude/Codex/Gemini/etc.) and converts them through a canonical intermediate representation, then writes to target native formats, with atomic write and conflict handling.\n\n## Session Resume in Codex CLI\n\n/resume is a slash command inside a running session that opens a saved-session picker, allowing you to select a past session and Codex reloads the transcript, letting you continue from where you left off.\n\nWhen you reopen a session, the model reads the transcript history to reconstruct context, rather than resuming from an actual saved model state. The conversation is preserved; the model's internal \"memory\" of working through the problem is reconstructed from the record.\n\n## Other Cross-Tool Options\n\n**continues** can be run via npx without installation, automatically discovers and parses each tool's native format (JSONL, JSON, SQLite, YAML), extracts recent messages, file changes, and tool activity, then generates a handoff document injected into the target tool so the receiving agent understands what was being done.\n\n**authsec-bridge** reads your Claude Code / Codex / Gemini session from disk, transforms it into the target CLI's exact session schema, and drops it into the target's session folder so the target's native --resume flow finds the conversation as if you'd had it there all along.\n\n\nREMINDE