{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"commit 6526090feef56b39f756077ad43d4692f53a3ccf\nAuthor: Evin Tunador <evintunador@gmail.com>\nDate:   Mon Jul 20 11:44:47 2026 -0700\n\n    Re-normalize preserved unrecognized events (0.6.0)\n    \n    `cledger renormalize` (library `renormalize()`) turns each preserved\n    `unrecognized` event this version can now interpret into the proper\n    `conversation_turn`, appending a `supersession` event linking the two so\n    consumers see the interpreted turn instead of the raw placeholder. This is\n    the supersession half of the format-drift roadmap item; preservation shipped\n    in 0.5.0.\n    \n    Id fidelity is the crux: each adapter exposes `renormalizeUnrecognized`,\n    which re-feeds the stored `raw.data` through the same `convertLine` the live\n    capture loop uses, with the identity-determining inputs recovered from the\n    preserved event (seq, session id, and — for a timestampless codex line —\n    occurred_at as the baseTime fallback). The turn therefore gets the exact id a\n    live capture would produce, so a later live capture dedups rather than\n    duplicating.\n    \n    Append-only and idempotent: the unrecognized event is never deleted, only\n    superseded; re-runs skip already-superseded targets and dedup on\n    deterministic ids. The reconstructed turn rides the normal appendEvents\n    redaction path (idempotent on already-redacted raw.data), and codex\n    `reasoning` can never reach this path, so nothing is re-exposed or\n    reconstructed. Manual-only for now; auto-triggering on a version bump is a\n    deferred follow-up.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n README.md                    |  19 +++--\n docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md |  35 +++++++-\n package.json                 |   2 +-\n src/adapters/claude-code.ts  |  27 +++++-\n src/adapters/codex.ts        |  35 +++++++-\n src/cli.ts                   |  16 ++++\n src/index.ts             